SENTINEL Donkey Race README
---------------------------

Welcome to the Donkey Race game!
Donkey Race is a simple driving game for the reZet80 SENTINEL.
The game "Donkey" was first written in BASIC in 1981 for the IBM PC DOS by
Bill Gates and Neil Konzen.
I have completely rewritten the game in Assembler.
To start the game enter "DR" at the prompt and press ENTER.
The display reads "DONKEY RACE". Press any key to begin.

You are driving on a two-lane road from left to right.
A donkey appears randomly on one side of the road.
Change lanes in good time to avoid the donkey (press the ENTER key to do so).
As the car avoids the donkey, it moves to the right.
The donkey is getting faster and faster.
If you manage to reach the right-hand side of the screen you can continue your
race on the left-hand side.
If your car hits the donkey "BOOM!" will be displayed and the game is over.
Press ESC to quit the game or any other key to restart.

Enjoy!

